          "questionnaire.question.bluthochdruck.text": "Have you been diagnosed with high blood pressure by a doctor, or do you take blood pressure medication?",
          "questionnaire.question.coping.text": "Even in stressful situations, I find ways to cope.",
          "questionnaire.question.einbeinstand.help": "1 – Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart.\n2 – Focus your eyes on one point.\n3 – Lift one leg so that your foot is no longer touching the floor.\n4 – Maintain your balance for as long as possible.\n\nStop the timer as soon as the raised foot touches the floor.\n\nRepeat the test with each leg and record your best result. A large difference between the two legs may indicate a trainable difference.\n\n<b>What the single-leg stance test shows:<\/b>\nUnder the described eyes-open conditions, this test provides a guide to your static balance and coordination. Regular practice can help improve balance and make everyday movements safer. The test does not replace a medical assessment.",
          "questionnaire.question.einbeinstand.help_title": "How to perform the single-leg stance test correctly",
          "questionnaire.question.einbeinstand.placeholder": "e.g. 30",
          "questionnaire.question.einbeinstand.text": "How long can you stand on one leg without holding on to anything? (optional)",
