          "questionnaire.question.groesse.unit": "cm",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.help": "Exercises that strengthen the muscles using weights, equipment or your own body weight (e.g. push-ups, squats or weight training).\n\n<b>WHO recommendation:<\/b> At least twice a week for all major muscle groups.",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.help_title": "What is strength training?",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.option.tage0": "0 days",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.option.tage1": "1 day",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.option.tage2": "2 days",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.option.tage3plus": "3 days or more",
          "questionnaire.question.krafttraining.text": "On how many days per week do you do strength training?",
          "questionnaire.question.liegestuetze.help": "<b>The same standard technique applies to all genders:<\/b>\n1 – Lie face down, place your hands about shoulder-width apart and support yourself on your toes.\n2 – Straighten your arms; your body should form a straight line from head to heels.\n3 – Lower your body under control until your chest nearly touches the floor and your elbows are bent to at least about 90°.\n4 – Push all the way back up to the starting position.\n\nRepeat without a break while maintaining correct form. Stop the test as soon as you can no longer correct your technique after one cue.\n\n<b>What the push-up test shows:<\/b>\nPush-ups measure the muscular endurance of your chest, shoulders, arms and core. Strong upper-body muscles are important for everyday activities such as carrying or getting up and help prevent injuries from falls.",
          "questionnaire.question.liegestuetze.help_title": "How to perform the push-up test correctly",
          "questionnaire.question.liegestuetze.placeholder": "e.g. 15",
          "questionnaire.question.liegestuetze.text": "How many push-ups can you perform correctly without a break? (optional)",
          "questionnaire.question.liegestuetze.unit": "repetitions",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.help": "Omega-3 fatty acids from marine sources support your brain and heart and have a strong anti-inflammatory effect throughout the body. Because the body cannot produce enough of them itself, it is important to obtain them regularly through food. Algal oil is an excellent vegan alternative to fish. Your body can use it directly, unlike omega-3 precursors from other plant oils.",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.help_title": "Why is omega-3 important?",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.option.nie": "Never",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.option.u1woche": "Less than once per week",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.option.ue2": "More than twice per week",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.option.w1": "Once per week",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.option.w2": "Twice per week",
          "questionnaire.question.omega3.text": "How often per week do you eat oily fish (e.g. salmon, mackerel or herring) or take an omega-3 supplement?",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.help": "<b>Vegetables &amp; salads:<\/b> spinach, broccoli, carrots, tomatoes, cucumbers, peppers, onions, garlic\n<b>Fruit:<\/b> apples, bananas, berries, oranges, grapes, avocado\n<b>Grains &amp; pseudograins:<\/b> oats, quinoa, millet, buckwheat, barley, brown rice\n<b>Seeds:<\/b> chia seeds, linseeds, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds, sesame seeds\n<b>Legumes &amp; nuts:<\/b> lentils, chickpeas, beans, almonds, walnuts\n<b>Spices &amp; herbs:<\/b> basil, oregano, turmeric, ginger, cinnamon, pepper\n<b>Mushrooms:<\/b> button mushrooms, shiitake, oyster mushrooms\n\n<b>Why is plant diversity important?<\/b>\nA colourful variety of plants provides nutrients, antioxidants and fibre. Each plant contains its own bioactive compounds that support different functions in the body. Diversity particularly supports the gut microbiome and thereby promotes a healthy intestinal flora.",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.help_title": "What counts as a plant food, for example?",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.option.u10": "Fewer than 10",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.option.ue35": "35 or more",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.option.v10_17": "10–17",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.option.v18_25": "18–25",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.option.v26_34": "26–34",
          "questionnaire.question.pflanzenvielfalt.text": "How many different plant foods did you eat in the past week?",
          "questionnaire.question.positive_emotionen.text": "I regularly experience moments of joy or gratitude in my daily life.",
          "questionnaire.question.protein.help": "This question assesses how regularly you include sources of protein. It does <b>not<\/b> calculate how many grams of protein you actually consume per day and per kilogram of body weight.\n\n<b>Suitable sources of protein include:<\/b>\n• Legumes such as lentils, beans or chickpeas\n• Tofu, tempeh, eggs, quark, yoghurt or cottage cheese\n• Fish or meat\n<b>Guidance for regular strength training:<\/b>\nFor healthy adults, around 1.4–1.6 g of protein per kg of body weight per day is a practical guide. In a large meta-analysis, the average additional benefits for building lean mass levelled off markedly from around 1.6 g/kg/day. This is not a strict biological limit.\n\nUp to around 2.0 g/kg/day may be appropriate on an individual basis during very high training loads or a deliberate energy deficit. Most people do not need this amount, and age alone is not a reason to aim for 2.0 g/kg/day. Strength training provides the training stimulus; protein provides the building blocks. Protein powder is not automatically necessary.\n\nPeople under the age of 18 and those with kidney disease or a medically prescribed diet should discuss the appropriate amount with a healthcare professional.",
          "questionnaire.question.protein.help_title": "What does this question measure, and how much is appropriate?",
