          "sources.blood_pressure.point.1": "Hypertension is defined as 140/90 mmHg or higher when measured on two different days.",
          "sources.blood_pressure.point.2": "Very high readings (~180/120 mmHg) → prompt medical assessment.",
          "sources.blood_pressure.point.3": "The target is often below 130/80 mmHg for people at higher risk, and otherwise below 140/90.",
          "sources.blood_pressure.point.4": "Lifestyle changes can lower blood pressure; alcohol: no more than 1 drink/day for women or 2 for men.",
          "sources.blood_pressure.reference": "WHO – Hypertension",
          "sources.blood_pressure.title": "Blood pressure & cardiovascular prevention",
